# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which does NOT exclude
# public/ — so every build would upload the full 64 MB regulatory corpus to reach
# the one 14 MB file the image actually needs.
#
# Keep in step with .dockerignore: this decides what leaves the machine, that
# decides what the Docker daemon sees. Anything dropped here can never be COPYed,
# so the rag-chunks re-include below is load-bearing.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
*/node_modules
server/lib
server/tests
server/coverage
dist
dev-dist
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
.github
.claude
android
ios
apple
archive
e2e
/src
/tests
/scripts
screenshots
supabase
worker
*.log

# public/ is 64 MB and the image needs exactly one file from it.
# To re-include a file in an excluded directory, must re-include the directory path first.
public/
!public/data/
!public/data/rag-chunks.json
